        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "I could not verify whether an event was created after Pending Close because the event-level supporting records are restricted to the records-custodian role. My read attempt was denied, and the analyst-readable records contain no cost-event rows. I did not change any records.\n\nThe public records identify the work order as **WO-2025-09-004 / MO-25-09-1070** at Modine’s Racine site, in the September cost period. That period entered Pending Close at **2025-09-30T18:00:00**. The public records do not provide the event’s source transaction ID, amount, creation time, or accounting status, so I can’t calculate how late it was or assess the recorded status for this event.\n\nThe supplied Oracle 26B guidance says that new transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are not staged for accounting until the period is closed or reopened, subject to stated exceptions. Without the event details, I can’t determine whether that treatment applies here or whether its recorded status is consistent. I submitted an incomplete report marked as needing evidence and escalated the access limitation to the supervisor.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
